window.docContents[216].resolve({"/Types-and-expressions/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions":{"contents":"The typing and evaluation rules of the basic constructions of Expr. The typing rules are constructors of Semantics.HasType and Semantics.LHasType, which Typing.expr and Typing.lval implement. The evaluation rules are constructors of Semantics.Eval and Semantics.LEval, which Eval.expr and Eval.lval implement, each rule in the comment of the case that implements it. Calls, lambdas, this, members and the uses of the library have their rules in the later chapters.\n\nWhere C++17 leaves the evaluation order unspecified, Core C++ evaluates left to right. The last section holds the composite and recursive types, objects and pointers, whose expressions denote locations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Core C++","header":"3. Types and expressions","id":"/Types-and-expressions/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions"}});